{
  "slug": "tokalator-glossary",
  "name": "Tokalator Glossary",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Auto-generates a codebase glossary (symbol index) after /init or on demand. Scans Python, JavaScript, and TypeScript files using AST parsing to map every class, function, and export with file path and line number. The glossary acts as a compressed context layer , Claude can consult it instead of reading files, saving thousands of tokens per session.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `glossary` (Generate a full codebase glossary (symbol index) for the current project), `glossary-lookup` (Look up a symbol in the codebase glossary — pass symbol name as argument), `glossary-refresh` (Refresh the codebase glossary after code changes), `glossary-stats` (Show codebase statistics from the glossary — files, symbols, refactor candidates)\n- **Hooks** (1): `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install tokalator-glossary@claude-community` from `vfaraji89/tokalator-glossary`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 4,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
